  "enable": false,
  "reason": "every bank-tile input lands in an RTL flop and every output is a flop: the chain pins in the CPI/CPO face registers (HH-9), the write/beat pins in the landing/write-port flops; a kit flop stage would shift the compiled systolic schedule"
 },
 "structural_change": "HBM-COLLECT10/COL-HC 10-21 cbrw8: cb_rw6 / cb_rw6m (339c0ce3a, ep5) CTS FAIL clk_c pin-flop spread 127.4 / 127.9 ps TT (263 internal sinks). Sink dump: chain cd/cv wraps lane leaf g0 (W channel x 8..43 at the d_* pins + S strip y 6..43 at the o_* pins), taps cv[3..8] / cd[*][27] dragged to x 185, fin_q / f_o relaying f_in (NW) -> f_out (SE) at (188, 230). rw8 RTL (0 added edges, same registers / ages): row assembler split by stage over two regional roots: h on clk_d<r>, a + bad on clk_h<r> (NEW port per row); x write copies on their x SRAM's root clk_x<r>; weight write copies on WR 3 (MAIN) their SRAM pair's read root clk_w<r> / WR 4 (FALLBACK) clk_h<r>. cb: FQR 1 = fin_q / f_o on their own 2-sink root clk_f (NEW port); the cv / cd chain fenced (dbRegion, released before DPL/CTS by tools/landed_parent/lp_fence_release.tcl) beside the d_* / o_* pins: MAIN SW corner box, FALLBACK W-channel box at the d_* pins. MAIN (WR 3).",
 "job": {
  "owner": "Claude:HBM-COLLECT10/COL-HC",
  "branch": "claude/hcbank-rw8-1021",
  "tag": "cbrw8",
  "purpose": "HC bank cb cbrw8: row assembler h/a regional roots + copies on SRAM roots (rw8), 0 added edges",
